        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is the issue with LazyVim, not 'mini.starter'. The message goes away if `{ import = \"lazyvim.plugins.extras.ui.mini-starter\" },` line is removed. There is [this call](https://github.com/LazyVim/LazyVim/blob/2e1c945f61821eec818a1512bc05b45366c0dfeb/lua/lazyvim/plugins/extras/ui/mini-starter.lua#L71) in 'lazyvim.plugins.extras.ui.mini-starter' which does not guard against the appeared message because it is not an error.\r\n\r\nI think the suggested solution is to remove `{ import = \"lazyvim.plugins.extras.ui.mini-starter\" },` from the config as you mostly have 'mini.starter' setup in your config.\r\n\r\nClosing as not an issue with 'mini.starter'.",
